Nested Class in C++

📌 Description

This C++ program demonstrates the concept of a Nested Class.

The "Department" class is defined inside the "University" class and is used to store and display the department name.

---

🧠 Concepts Used

- Classes and Objects
- Nested Class
- Constructors
- Encapsulation
- "std::string"
- "std::move()"
- Scope Resolution Operator "::"

---

⚙️ Working

The program works as follows:

1. "University" is the outer class.
2. "Department" is a class defined inside "University".
3. The "Department" class contains a private "name" variable.
4. Its constructor initializes the department name.
5. The "display()" function prints the department name.
6. The nested class object is created using:
   University::Department

---

🖥️ Sample Output

Department: Artificial Intelligence and Data Science

