🧠 OOP Concept Used

Nested Class

A nested class is a class declared inside another class.

In this program:

class University {
    class Department {
        // ...
    };
};

The "Department" class is nested inside the "University" class.

The nested class can be accessed using the scope resolution operator "::":

University::Department

---

🎯 Objective

To understand how a nested class can be declared inside another class and accessed using the scope resolution operator "::".

